The pymolish-studio icon and logo
=================================

Files: pymolish.png and logo.png in this folder, docs/img/logo-dark.png,
and copies of them in other sizes or file formats.

The icon and the logo are the marks of the pymolish-studio project: they
tell people that a program or a page is pymolish-studio. They were generated
with ChatGPT for this project and belong to Adrian Jasinski, the author of
pymolish-studio.

They are NOT under the MIT license of the code (LICENSE-MIT) and not under
the Open-Source PyMOL license (LICENSE). All rights are reserved, except
for the permissions below.

You may, without asking:

- copy and pass on the files unchanged, together with pymolish-studio: in
  its source code, in its downloadable builds, in packages of it whose
  changes are limited to what packaging needs, and in mirrors;
- use them unchanged to refer to pymolish-studio: in articles, talks,
  teaching material, lists of software and links to the project.

You may not, without written permission:

- use them, or an image that can be confused with them, as the icon or logo
  of another program. A changed version of pymolish-studio that you give to
  others is another program in this sense: give it its own icon and logo,
  as it needs its own name;
- change them, other than resizing them or converting the file format;
- use them in a way that suggests that the pymolish-studio project or its
  author made, supports or recommends your product or service.

Nothing here limits what the two code licenses allow you to do with the
code, and nothing here limits uses that the law allows anyway.

PyMOL is a trademark of Schrodinger, LLC. This notice makes no claim to it.
